    {
      "id": "r20261025-a02",
      "title": "Why Boredom Can Be Good for You",
      "level": "Menengah atas",
      "min": 4,
      "body": [
        "These days, it is almost impossible to feel bored. The moment we wait in a line or sit on a bus, we reach for our phones. But psychologists say that a little boredom is actually good for us.",
        "When the brain has nothing to do, it starts to wander. During this wandering, people often have their most creative ideas. Many writers and inventors say their best ideas came when they were doing something boring, like walking or washing dishes.",
        "Boredom also teaches children an important skill: how to entertain themselves. A child who is never bored may struggle when there is no screen or toy available. So next time you feel bored, do not reach for your phone immediately. Give your mind a few quiet minutes, and see where it takes you."
      ],
      "gloss": {
        "almost": "hampir",
        "reach": "meraih",
        "wander": "mengembara",
        "inventors": "penemu",
        "skill": "keterampilan",
        "available": "tersedia",
        "immediately": "segera"
      },
      "qs": [
        {
          "q": "What happens when the brain has nothing to do?",
          "opts": [
            "It starts to wander",
            "It falls asleep",
            "It forgets everything"
